! MULTIPLOT: a page of subplots.  Each analysis fills the next cell (or the
! SUBPLOT one); the GO with nothing open draws the page.  The page's
! commands are recorded (they redraw it on a lens change) and listed last.
RES osdtriplet
FFO -0.1
IFO 0.025
NFO 5
MULTIPLOT 3 2 'Triplet at paraxial focus'
SUBPLOT 1 1
RIM ; GO
SUBPLOT 1 2
MTF ; MFR 200 ; IFR 10 ; GO
SUBPLOT 2 1 1 2
SPO THF ; ORI H ; RECTDENS 6 ; GO
SUBPLOT 3 1
MTF THF ; FRE 100 ; NRD 32 ; GO
SUBPLOT 3 2
FIE ; GO
GO
! the listed commands draw the same page again (on one line, as a redraw
! runs them)
MULTIPLOT 3 2 'Triplet at paraxial focus'; SUBPLOT 1 1; RIM; GO; SUBPLOT 1 2; MTF; MFR 200; IFR 10; GO; SUBPLOT 2 1 1 2; SPO THF; ORI H; RECTDENS 6; GO; SUBPLOT 3 1; MTF THF; FRE 100; NRD 32; GO; SUBPLOT 3 2; FIE; GO; GO
! no SUBPLOT: cells fill by rows; a full page refuses more
MULTIPLOT 1 2
SPO ; RECTDENS 6 ; GO
MTF THF ; NRD 32 ; GO
PMA ; GO
GO
! bad input
SUBPLOT 1 1
MULTIPLOT 0 2
MULTIPLOT 2 7
MULTIPLOT 2 2 'no end
MULTIPLOT 2 2
SUBPLOT 3 1
SUBPLOT 1 2 1 2
SUBPLOT 1
MULTIPLOT 1 1
SINRAYTRA ; GO
GO
! the lens drawing is a subplot like any other
MULTIPLOT 1 2 'Layout and spots'
VIE ; GO
SPO ; RECTDENS 6 ; GO
GO
